[[{"str":"Yes/No/NG Questions Strategy Practice","x":134.19911262622878,"y":753.67506332,"width":328.59597982543426,"height":20.0117883352},{"str":"","x":107.34004995999999,"y":684.61712908,"width":0,"height":14.0067505752},{"str":"What is dopamine – and is it to blame for our addictions?","x":107.34004995999999,"y":684.61712908,"width":381.253433412378,"height":14.0067505752},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":650.83879168,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"The key difference between human brains and those of other animals is the size and","x":72.06045311999999,"y":650.83879168,"width":451.5624175151872,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"complexity","x":72.06045311999999,"y":634.3249378400001,"width":56.73118665674906,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":128.79163977674904,"y":634.3249378400001,"width":10.437505199999997,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"of","x":136.62634138252358,"y":634.3249378400001,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":146.64255664872323,"y":634.3249378400001,"width":10.437500079999962,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"our cerebral cortex, the brain’s outer layer of neural tissue. We","x":154.47725441127358,"y":634.3249378400001,"width":369.2394507037502,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"therefore tend to focus our attention on this area, believing that our unique mental","x":72.06045311999999,"y":617.811084,"width":451.25161549644747,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"life is due to this masterpiece of evolution. However, we often ignore the bits that are","x":72.06045311999999,"y":601.29723016,"width":451.5330960567625,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"nearly identical between humans and animals, such as the tiny group of brain cells","x":72.06045311999999,"y":584.78337632,"width":451.3864925478119,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"that use the chemical dopamine to communicate with other brain cells.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":568.26952248,"width":381.28471196184995,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":453.34516508184976,"y":568.26952248,"width":4.437505040000047,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Dopamine is","x":456.6760882475236,"y":568.26952248,"width":66.74739651841486,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":551.7556686400001,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"often described as the brain’s “pleasure chemical”, but it is actually involved in a","x":72.06045311999999,"y":551.7556686400001,"width":451.6034732977983,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"large number of physical and mental processes. It is used by a cluster of neurons in","x":72.06045311999999,"y":535.2418148,"width":451.357167306213,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"the midbrain to transmit messages to other neurons. The dopamine neurons are","x":72.06045311999999,"y":518.72796096,"width":451.4627245205124,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"small in number (~0.0006% of the neurons in the human brain) and they are","x":72.06045311999999,"y":502.21410712000005,"width":451.5448283992865,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"observed in all mammals and even “simple” animals such as turtles.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":485.70025328,"width":360.44887151096594,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"In the 1950s, researchers discovered that rats appeared to enjoy the stimulation of","x":72.06045311999999,"y":454.92443476000005,"width":451.39822296872336,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"the nerve bundle that links the dopamine neurons with their targets in the forebrain.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":438.41058092000003,"width":451.73834806724807,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"The rats would learn to press a lever for this kind of stimulation, and, left unchecked,","x":72.06045311999999,"y":421.89672708,"width":451.6855694300732,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"would do so thousands of times in a day. A similar (and wholly unethical) experiment","x":72.06045311999999,"y":405.38287324000004,"width":451.52136917882314,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"was performed in 1970 on a human patient. Like the rats, the patient learned to","x":72.06045311999999,"y":388.8690194,"width":451.39822296872336,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"press a button to stimulate the dopamine nerve bundle, pressing the button up to","x":72.06045311999999,"y":372.35516556000005,"width":451.0815473024498,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"1500","x":72.06045311999999,"y":355.84131172,"width":26.717726416098866,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":98.77817953609885,"y":355.84131172,"width":10.437500240000013,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"times","x":106.61287741874999,"y":355.84131172,"width":28.693993830874525,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":135.30687124962452,"y":355.84131172,"width":10.43749759999999,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"over","x":143.14156715061318,"y":355.84131172,"width":23.363349914899246,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":166.50491706551244,"y":355.84131172,"width":10.437500160000006,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"the","x":174.3396148881132,"y":355.84131172,"width":16.69564687022434,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":191.03526175833755,"y":355.84131172,"width":10.437502639999979,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"course of a three-hour session and reporting feelings of","x":198.8699614425,"y":355.84131172,"width":324.4010572162236,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"pleasure during the stimulation.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":339.32745788000005,"width":166.90369030527006,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Since then, studies have shown that the dopamine system can be activated by a","x":72.06045311999999,"y":308.5516393600001,"width":451.31025481027484,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"wide range of pleasant experiences, such as eating, sexual intercourse, getting","x":72.06045311999999,"y":292.03778552000006,"width":451.4099495464106,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"revenge, winning video games, listening to music, earning money and reading funny","x":72.06045311999999,"y":275.52393168000003,"width":451.0815509655228,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"cartoons. The dopamine system also responds robustly to addictive drugs, including","x":72.06045311999999,"y":259.01007784,"width":451.14019388237244,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"opiates, alcohol and cocaine. These drugs can evoke stronger activation than natural","x":72.06045311999999,"y":242.4962240000001,"width":451.2633384110619,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"rewards and, unlike natural rewards, they do not cause satiety. A straightforward","x":72.06045311999999,"y":225.98237016000007,"width":451.19883475750925,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"interpretation of these facts is that the dopamine system is a pleasure pathway in the","x":72.06045311999999,"y":209.46851632000005,"width":451.38062628647464,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"brain. This potentially explains why animals and people would be willing to press","x":72.06045311999999,"y":192.95466248000002,"width":451.2926618511492,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"buttons or push levers to activate the dopamine neurons. It might also explain why","x":72.06045311999999,"y":176.44080864,"width":451.5506946606235,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"some drugs are so addictive. The strong and prolonged activation induced by drugs","x":72.06045311999999,"y":159.9269548000001,"width":451.49204970206074,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"can act as a “super-reward”, making drugs even more desirable.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":143.41310096000007,"width":341.1084274214146,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"However, many mental events occur near the time of a reward, including changes in","x":72.06045311999999,"y":112.63728244000004,"width":451.77939652371333,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"motivation, arousal, attention, emotion, and learning. For example, imagine passing","x":72.06045311999999,"y":96.12342860000001,"width":451.5741460745371,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"by a vending machine that offers sweets. If you are motivated by hunger, your","x":72.06045311999999,"y":79.6095747600001,"width":451.44513726617294,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":44.32997792000003,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Note: This is not a real IELTS test. This practice test is to give you an opportunity to practise","x":72.06045311999999,"y":44.32997792000003,"width":444.120631174785,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"implementing the strategies from the course. It does not reflect the scores, time needed or","x":72.06045311999999,"y":30.068013240000028,"width":444.4724880753799,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"level of difficulty of a real IELTS test.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":15.806048560000022,"width":176.13409149452846,"height":12.01007552}],[{"str":"Yes/No/NG Questions Strategy Practice","x":134.19911262622878,"y":753.67503776,"width":328.59597982543426,"height":20.0117883352},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":710.88914372,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"attention will be drawn to the machine and you will become more alert as you","x":72.06045311999999,"y":710.88914372,"width":451.18124215868636,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"approach it. Once you have eaten the sweets, you experience pleasure, your brain","x":72.06045311999999,"y":694.3752898800001,"width":451.32784758924913,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"learns to associate the vending machine with reward, and your hunger decreases. It","x":72.06045311999999,"y":677.8614360400001,"width":451.22815657623704,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"is likely that the dopamine system is involved in many of these processes rather than","x":72.06045311999999,"y":661.3475822,"width":451.351304767999,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"just pleasure per se.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":644.8337283600001,"width":108.14932211644678,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":614.0579098400001,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"One of the most important aspects of dopamine function is learning. Researchers","x":72.06045311999999,"y":614.0579098400001,"width":451.4568657054219,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"believe that dopamine neurons change their activity when expectations about reward","x":72.06045311999999,"y":597.544056,"width":451.43340486359875,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"do not match the reality, signalling a ‘reward prediction error’ that drives learning. For","x":72.06045311999999,"y":581.03020216,"width":451.2692046723992,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"instance, dopamine neurons are activated by unanticipated rewards, but they are","x":72.06045311999999,"y":564.5163483200001,"width":451.66797671114927,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"suppressed when expected rewards fail to materialise. Events followed by increases","x":72.06045311999999,"y":548.00249448,"width":451.7148928701606,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"in dopamine activation become associated with reward, and those that are followed","x":72.06045311999999,"y":531.4886406400001,"width":451.65624809174915,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"by decreases are linked with disappointment. If the environment is unchanging, all","x":72.06045311999999,"y":514.9747868,"width":451.7324878109486,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"our brains need to do to obtain reward is to engage in actions that activate the","x":72.06045311999999,"y":498.46093296000004,"width":451.39235862899807,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"dopamine neurons and avoid the ones that suppress them.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":481.9470791200001,"width":313.1357417920648,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"It is highly unlikely that we have much awareness of the learning that dopamine","x":72.06045311999999,"y":451.1712606000001,"width":451.21056343696023,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"activation induces, such as making us attached to things we unknowingly associate","x":72.06045311999999,"y":434.65740675999996,"width":451.6503818904619,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"with dopamine activation. This lack of awareness might explain why people often","x":72.06045311999999,"y":418.14355292000005,"width":451.7969930258108,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"make seemingly irrational or maladaptive choices. Imagine a drug addict taking","x":72.06045311999999,"y":401.62969908000014,"width":451.3688976670742,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"cocaine. Because the pleasure from cocaine does not satiate like a natural reward,","x":72.06045311999999,"y":385.11584524,"width":451.22815453452375,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"the dopamine activation, and hence drug-induced learning, occurs with each puff of","x":72.06045311999999,"y":368.6019914000001,"width":451.6797091137234,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"the crack pipe, making the actual pipe an object which the addict is drawn to.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":352.08813755999995,"width":407.9086081016388,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":321.31231904000015,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Can brain research be used to overcome the effects of dopamine in addiction?","x":72.06045311999999,"y":321.31231904000015,"width":451.80872152511023,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Neuroscientists are actively pursuing the creation of drugs that block the learning","x":72.06045311999999,"y":304.7984652,"width":451.7148890869866,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"induced by dopamine in addiction. However, they have had limited success, for it is","x":72.06045311999999,"y":288.2846113600001,"width":451.7031644909621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"difficult to create a drug that blocks the learning without also blocking other functions","x":72.06045311999999,"y":271.77075751999996,"width":451.6445213339107,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"of dopamine, such as feeling alert, motivated and happy. Dopamine-induced learning","x":72.06045311999999,"y":255.25690368000005,"width":451.26920269073685,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"is certainly not the whole story behind addiction, but it does suggest that we should","x":72.06045311999999,"y":238.74304984000014,"width":451.1460544389239,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"consider whether addiction is something that human reasoning on its own can","x":72.06045311999999,"y":222.229196,"width":451.47445313991267,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"overcome.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":205.7153421600001,"width":56.068521251973394,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":128.12897437197338,"y":205.7153421600001,"width":10.437497840000008,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"The","x":135.9636704531132,"y":205.7153421600001,"width":20.695095817074147,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":156.65876627018736,"y":205.7153421600001,"width":10.43750767999997,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"same","x":164.49346973752358,"y":205.7153421600001,"width":29.368387674899243,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":193.8618574124228,"y":205.7153421600001,"width":10.437500160000006,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"might very well also apply to other everyday failures of","x":201.69655523502357,"y":205.7153421600001,"width":322.1022461924263,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"willpower, such as overeating. Our special cerebral cortex may be in control of our","x":72.06045311999999,"y":189.20148831999995,"width":451.5858803386728,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"actions, but our primitive dopamine system may very well serve as its teacher.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":172.68763448000004,"width":414.50593979021477,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":141.91181596,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Source:","x":72.06045311999999,"y":141.91181596,"width":41.39019175424906,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"http://theconversation.com/explainer-what-is-dopamine-and-is-it-to-blame-for-our-ad","x":72.06045311999999,"y":125.3979621200001,"width":445.897508636886,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"dictions-51268","x":72.06045311999999,"y":108.88410827999996,"width":78.11826915687263,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":44.32995236000011,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Note: This is not a real IELTS test. This practice test is to give you an opportunity to practise","x":72.06045311999999,"y":44.32995236000011,"width":444.120631174785,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"implementing the strategies from the course. It does not reflect the scores, time needed or","x":72.06045311999999,"y":30.067987679999987,"width":444.4724880753799,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"level of difficulty of a real IELTS test.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":15.806023000000096,"width":176.13409149452846,"height":12.01007552}],[{"str":"Yes/No/NG Questions Strategy Practice","x":134.19911262622878,"y":753.6750122000001,"width":328.59597982543426,"height":20.0117883352},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":710.88911816,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Questions 1-10","x":72.06045311999999,"y":710.88911816,"width":86.0995740914468,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":694.37526432,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Do the following statements agree with the claims of the writer in the passage?","x":72.06045311999999,"y":694.37526432,"width":417.90136624913873,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":661.34755664,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Yes","x":72.06045311999999,"y":661.34755664,"width":21.369489781199622,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":93.42994290119961,"y":661.34755664,"width":4.445312560000011,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"if the statement agrees with the claims of the writer","x":96.7667266234249,"y":661.34755664,"width":270.3439839527929,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":644.8337028000001,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"No","x":72.06045311999999,"y":644.8337028000001,"width":16.00952446684981,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":88.0699775868498,"y":644.8337028000001,"width":4.445312520000009,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"if the statement contradicts the claims of the writer","x":91.4067612790499,"y":644.8337028000001,"width":267.0013360109432,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":628.31984896,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Not Given","x":72.06045311999999,"y":628.31984896,"width":56.71945797729849,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":128.7799110972985,"y":628.31984896,"width":4.445312799999974,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this","x":132.1166949996749,"y":628.31984896,"width":294.36999939256856,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":590.0377332400001,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"1.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":590.0377332400001,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":590.0377332400001,"width":4.4453130799999965,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"There are many ways in which human brains differ from the brains of other","x":85.41345249875235,"y":590.0377332400001,"width":395.8457538243632,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"animals.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":573.5238794000002,"width":44.72111113674906,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":557.01002556,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"2.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":557.01002556,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":557.01002556,"width":4.4453130799999965,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"The cells in the brain that make use of dopamine as a means of communication","x":85.41345249875235,"y":557.01002556,"width":421.9125436352376,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"are unique to humans.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":540.4961717200001,"width":119.51432507069589,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":523.98231788,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"3.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":523.98231788,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":523.98231788,"width":4.4453125599999925,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Dopamine can be characterised in other ways than as simply a chemical involved","x":85.41345210842489,"y":523.98231788,"width":431.9111663026141,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"in the sensation of pleasure.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":507.4684640400001,"width":150.2256362740704,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":490.95461020000016,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"4.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":490.95461020000016,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":490.95461020000016,"width":4.4453125599999925,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"The experiment carried out on a human subject in 1970 was unethical because it","x":85.41345210842489,"y":490.95461020000016,"width":428.6154323579619,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"lasted for 3 hours.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":474.44075636000025,"width":96.13338231677189,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":457.9269025200001,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"5.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":457.9269025200001,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":457.9269025200001,"width":4.4453130799999965,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"A possible explanation for the addictiveness of some drugs is that they cause a","x":85.41345249875235,"y":457.9269025200001,"width":419.93041218098864,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"big stimulation of the dopamine neurons and this leads to a big feeling of pleasure.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":441.41304868,"width":437.9865751785113,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":424.8991948400003,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"6.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":424.8991948400003,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":424.8991948400003,"width":4.4453125599999925,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"People who are hungry are more affected by the feeling of alertness than the","x":85.41345210842489,"y":424.8991948400003,"width":407.9320649801368,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"feeling of pleasure.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":408.38534100000015,"width":101.4874833514468,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":391.87148716,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"7","x":72.06045311999999,"y":391.87148716,"width":6.679431604024717,"height":12.01007552},{"str":". The more an expectation of being rewarded is not met, the more the dopamine","x":78.73988514437735,"y":391.87148716,"width":424.5983903318861,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"neurons in the brain are activated.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":375.3576333199999,"width":181.59961264201914,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":358.8437794800002,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"8.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":358.8437794800002,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":358.8437794800002,"width":4.4453125599999925,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Most people are probably very conscious of the process of learning that is brought","x":85.41345210842489,"y":358.8437794800002,"width":435.9458006873117,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"about by means of dopamine in the brain.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":342.32992564000006,"width":220.99594414246778,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":325.8160717999999,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"9.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":325.8160717999999,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":82.07666838619961,"y":325.8160717999999,"width":4.4453125599999925,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Someone who is addicted to cocaine may well be attracted to the physical pipe","x":85.41345210842489,"y":325.8160717999999,"width":418.59335305228893,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"they use to smoke the substance as well as to the substance itself.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":309.30221796000023,"width":354.4907481084659,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":292.7883641200001,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"10.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":292.7883641200001,"width":16.69564687022434,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":88.75609999022433,"y":292.7883641200001,"width":4.44531312,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"A problem which arises for scientists working on dopamine is that it is easier to","x":92.09288413280225,"y":292.7883641200001,"width":417.86618069119004,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"create a drug that blocks the happiness function of dopamine than one that blocks"